        "DateText": "ca 1560; ca.1619-before1686",
        "Notes": "Created in the second half of the 16th century as Accademia degli Accesi. Restored ca 1619 as Accademia dei Ravvivati, with motto `Un fiato sol che spira`, and emblem representing `Burning logs, blown on by a wind`  (see Branchi`s Clorinda). From 1636 it was called Accademia dei Riaccesi, with the above motto and emblem. Possibly, the following volume - not in British Library collections - belongs to this Academy: Costante Accademico Travagliato, Lagrime del Reno di Bologna rime funebri, nella infelicissima morte dell`illustre sig. conte Andalo Bentivogli vcciso a caso giostrando. Del Costante Academico Trauagliato (In Bologna: per Vittorio Benacci, 1590).",
